# EC2 Deployment Documentation

## SkillBridge About Page Deployment, Start, Stop, Create, and Update Scenarios

This documentation explains what to do in every common situation when using the GitHub Actions workflows for deploying the About Page to AWS EC2.

---

# 1. Workflows Used

You should have two GitHub Actions workflow files:

```text
.github/workflows/deploy-about-page.yml
.github/workflows/stop-ec2.yml
```

## Workflow 1: Deploy About Page

Name in GitHub Actions:

```text
Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

This workflow is used to:

```text
Create a new EC2 instance if none exists
Start the stopped EC2 instance if it already exists
Attach/reuse the Elastic IP
Install/configure Nginx and HTTPS when setup_server=true
Upload the latest website files from the selected branch
Reload Nginx
```

## Workflow 2: Stop EC2

Name in GitHub Actions:

```text
Stop AWS EC2 Instance
```

This workflow is used to:

```text
Pause/stop the EC2 instance
Keep the EC2 instance saved
Keep the files on the server
Keep the Elastic IP
Avoid deleting the server
```

---

# 2. Important Concepts

## EC2 Instance

The EC2 instance is your virtual server.

It runs:

```text
Ubuntu
Nginx
Your deployed HTML website
Certbot / Let’s Encrypt certificate
```

## Elastic IP

The Elastic IP is a fixed public IP address.

You need it because a normal EC2 public IP can change after stopping and starting the server.

With Elastic IP:

```text
Stop EC2
Start EC2 again
Same public IP stays
DuckDNS still points correctly
HTTPS still uses the same domain
```

## DuckDNS Domain

Your free domain is:

```text
skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

It should point to your Elastic IP.

Example:

```text
skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org → 12.34.56.78
```

## setup_server Input

This input controls whether the workflow configures the server.

```text
setup_server=true
```

Use this when:

```text
First time setting up the EC2 server
Setting up HTTPS
Changing domain
Fixing Nginx or Certbot
Creating a brand-new EC2 instance
```

```text
setup_server=false
```

Use this when:

```text
Server is already configured
You only want to upload new website files
You are deploying updates after stopping/starting the server
```

