# 3. First-Time Setup Scenario

Use this when the EC2 server does not exist yet.

## Step 1: Run Deploy Without Domain

Go to:

```text
GitHub Repository → Actions → Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2 → Run workflow
```

Use these values:

```text
setup_server: true          #   Install/configure Nginx and HTTPS on EC2 before deploy
deploy_branch: main   #       Branch or ref to deploy, e.g. main or gaurav-about-page write name of branch from where to upload 
deploy_domain: leave empty        #Optional domain, e.g. skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org. Leave empty for first HTTP-only setup.

``` 

This will:

```text
Create the EC2 instance
Create or reuse the security group
Create or reuse the key pair
Allocate an Elastic IP
Attach the Elastic IP to EC2
Install Nginx
Configure HTTP
Deploy the About Page files
Print the Elastic IP
```

At the end of the workflow, copy:

```text
Elastic IP: x.x.x.x
```

Example:

```text
Elastic IP: 12.34.56.78
```

---

## Step 2: Add Elastic IP to DuckDNS

Go to DuckDNS.

Set:

```text
Domain: skillbridgeacademy
IP: your Elastic IP
```

Example:

```text
skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org → 12.34.56.78    #update in ivp4
```

Save/update DuckDNS.

Then test from your computer:

```bash
nslookup skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

It should show your Elastic IP.

---

## Step 3: Run Deploy Again With Domain

Run the deploy workflow again.

Use:

```text
setup_server: true
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

This will:

```text
Use the existing EC2 instance
Use the same Elastic IP
Configure Nginx for the DuckDNS domain
Request a Let’s Encrypt HTTPS certificate
Enable HTTPS
Deploy the website files again
```

After this, your website should work at:

```text
http://skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
https://skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

