# 4. Normal Future Deployment Scenario

Use this when the server already exists and HTTPS already works.

Example: you changed HTML files and want to upload the latest version.

Run:

```text
Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

Use:

```text
setup_server: false
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

This will:

```text
Find the existing EC2 instance
Start it if it is stopped
Use the same Elastic IP
Upload latest files from main branch
Replace old files in /var/www/about-page
Reload Nginx
```

Use this most of the time.

---

# 5. Deploying From a Different Branch

Use this when you want to deploy a feature branch instead of main.

Example branch:

```text
gaurav-about-page
```

Run:

```text
Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

Use:

```text
setup_server: false
deploy_branch: gaurav-about-page
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

This will deploy files from that branch.

Example behavior:

```text
deploy_branch: main
→ deploys main branch

deploy_branch: gaurav-about-page
→ deploys gaurav-about-page branch
```

---

# 6. Stopping the EC2 Instance

Use this when you are finished working and want to pause the server.

Run:

```text
Stop AWS EC2 Instance
```

Input:

```text
confirm_stop: STOP
```

This will:

```text
Stop the EC2 instance
Keep the EC2 instance saved
Keep the website files
Keep Nginx installed
Keep Certbot installed
Keep the Elastic IP allocated
Keep DuckDNS pointing to the same IP
```

While the EC2 instance is stopped, the website will be offline.

This URL will not load while stopped:

```text
https://skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

That is normal.

---

# 7. Starting the EC2 Instance Again After Stopping

You do not need a separate “start” workflow.

To start the server again, run the deploy workflow.

Run:

```text
Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

Use:

```text
setup_server: false
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

This will:

```text
Find the stopped EC2 instance
Start it
Wait until it is ready
Reuse the same Elastic IP
Upload latest files
Reload Nginx
```

After the workflow finishes, the website should work again:

```text
https://skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

---

# 8. Updating the Website After Stopping

Scenario:

```text
You stopped the EC2 yesterday.
Today you changed files in GitHub.
You want the site online again with the new files.
```

Do this:

```text
Run Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

Use:

```text
setup_server: false
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

The workflow will:

```text
Start the stopped EC2
Get the latest files from main
Upload them to EC2
Reload Nginx
```

You do not need to update DuckDNS again.

---

# 9. Creating a New EC2 Instance

A new EC2 instance is created only when the workflow cannot find an existing instance with this name:

```text
skillbridge-about-page-server
```

The deploy workflow searches for an EC2 instance with this tag:

```text
Name = skillbridge-about-page-server
```

If found:

```text
It reuses the existing EC2 instance
```

If not found:

```text
It creates a new EC2 instance
```

A new EC2 instance may be created if:

```text
The old EC2 was terminated/deleted
The instance Name tag was changed
The instance is in another AWS region
The workflow is using a different AWS account
```

---

# 10. If EC2 Was Accidentally Terminated

If the EC2 instance was deleted/terminated, run:

```text
Provision and Deploy About Page to AWS EC2
```

Use:

```text
setup_server: true
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

The workflow will:

```text
Create a new EC2 instance
Attach the existing Elastic IP if it still exists
Install Nginx again
Configure HTTPS again
Deploy the website
```

If the Elastic IP still exists and DuckDNS already points to it, you do not need to change DuckDNS.

If a new Elastic IP is created, update DuckDNS with the new Elastic IP.

---

# 11. When to Use setup_server=true

Use:

```text
setup_server: true
```

for these scenarios:

```text
First-time setup
New EC2 instance was created
Nginx is not installed
HTTPS is not configured
Changing DuckDNS/domain name
Fixing broken Nginx config
Fixing broken Certbot config
Recreating certificate setup
```

Example:

```text
setup_server: true
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

---

# 12. When to Use setup_server=false

Use:

```text
setup_server: false
```

for normal deployments.

Use it when:

```text
EC2 already exists
Nginx already works
HTTPS already works
You only changed website files
You are deploying from main or another branch
You are starting the stopped server again
```

Example:

```text
setup_server: false
deploy_branch: main
deploy_domain: skillbridgeacademy.duckdns.org
```

This is the normal daily usage.

